#lem: X; X; mah[great]; An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; aya[father]; Nanna[1]DN; saŋ[head]; rig[donate]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.16

1.A.A.17. [X X] zalag#-ga ni₂ u₃-mu-ni-gid₂ ud-de₃ sa₂ i#-X-dug₄
#lem: X; X; zalag[bright]; ni[self]; gid[long]; ud[sun]; sa[equal]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: After you have extended yourself in the bright ……, the daylight ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.17

1.A.A.18. [...]-na šu gal du₈-a-bi ki-a u₃-mu-ni#-ge-en
#lem: X; šu[hand]; gal[big]; du[spread]; ki[place]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: after you have established …… on earth, on the day of the disappearance of the moon, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.18

1.A.A.19. [ud] nu₂-a itid šu du₇-a-zu uŋ₃-e u₃-X-pad₃
#lem: ud[sun]; nud[lie down]; itud[moon]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]; uŋ[people]; pad[find]
#tr.en: as you have completed the month, you summon (?) the people, lord; 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.19

1.A.A.20. en# kur-ra di gal mu-ku₅-re₆-en ka-aš mah# mu#-bar-re-en
#lem: en[lord]; kur[mountain(s)]; did[lawsuit]; gal[big]; kud[cut]; kaš[decision]; mah[great]; bar[place outside]
#tr.en: and then in the nether world you decree great judgments, you decide sublime verdicts. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.20

1.A.A.21. {d}en-ki {d}nin-ki en gal nun gal en nam [tar]-re-bi
#lem: Enkik[1]DN; Ninki[1 Ninki-goddess]; en[lord]; gal[big]; nun[prince]; gal[big]; en[lord]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enki} and @wDN{Ninki}, the great lords, the great princes, the lords who determine fates, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.21

1.A.A.22. e₃-a ka-za-ke₄ ša-ba-an-sug₂-ge-eš a-a ud-sakar# u₃-tud mu-ši-X-eš#
#lem: e[leave]; kag[mouth]; sug[stand]; aya[father]; udsakar[crescent moon]; utud[give birth (to)]; X
#tr.en: await your utterances, father; they …… the newborn (?) moon. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.22

1.A.A.23. nun niŋ₂-si-sa₂ ka-ga₁₄ i₃-ni-ŋar niŋ₂-du₇ pa bi₂#-e₃
#lem: nun[prince]; niŋsisa[justice]; kag[mouth]; ŋar[put]; niŋdu[that which is appropriate]; pa[branch]; e[leave]
#tr.en: Prince, you place justice in every mouth, and make propriety resplendent. Daily (?) you make hearts content, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.23

1.A.A.24. šag₄ ud mu-a-dug₃ nam ki-bi-še₃ ud mu-a-tar me-lem₄-zu# ud# MI X
#lem: šag[heart]; ud[sun]; dug[good]; nam[fate]; ki[place]; ud[sun]; tar[cut]; melim[frightening splendor]; ud[sun]; X; X
#tr.en: daily (?) you determine fates appropriately, daily (?) your refulgence ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.24

1.A.A.25. ŋiš-he₂ daŋal-la ŋir₂! ud mu-ni-bur₂ ku₁₀-ku₁₀# X mu-a-dadag
#lem: ŋešhe[firmament]; daŋal[wide]; ŋir[flash]; ud[sun]; bur[spread out]; kukkug[dark]; X; dadag[bright]
#tr.en: You brighten the night sky in the broad firmament, and illuminate the darkness. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.25

1.A.A.26. e₃-zu-še₃ sizkur₂ a-ra-zu-a {d}a-nun-na X im-ma-sug₂-sug₂-ge-eš
#lem: e[leave]; siškur[prayer]; arazu[supplication]; Anunak[1]DN; X; sug[stand]
#tr.en: The @wDN{Anuna} gods stand by with prayers and supplications at your rising. The sweet sight of your resplendent crescent, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.26

1.A.A.27. ud-sakar dalla e₃-a hi-li gur₃-ru u₆ di dug₃-ga-zu-še₃
#lem: udsakar[crescent moon]; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]; hili[attractiveness]; gur[lift]; u[admiration]; di[speak]; dug[good]
#tr.en: full of loveliness, brings joy to the great lady of the @wTN{Ki-ur}, Mother @wDN{Ninlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.27

1.A.A.28. nin gal ki-ur₃-ra ama {d}nin-lil₂ X-ra hul₂-la mu-ni-ib-DU
#lem: nin[lady]; gal[big]; Kiʾur[1]; ama[mother]; Ninlil[1]DN; X; hul[rejoice]; X
#tr.en: in ……, and the true and august lady, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.28

1.A.A.29. e₂-ŋa₂-ŋiš-šu₂-a ki-tuš! šag₄ hul₂-la# e₂#-gal ni₂ guru₃-na
#lem: Eŋaŋeššua[1]TN; kituš[dwelling place]; šag[heart]; hul[rejoice]; egal[palace]; ni[fear]; gur[lift]
#tr.en: the good cow, 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.29

1.A.A.30. nin zid mah ab₂ zid mas-su₂ A X [X X] X X a-ra-zu ša-ba-an-de₆
#lem: nin[lady]; zid[right]; mah[great]; ab[cow]; zid[right]; massu[leader]; X; X; X; X; X; X; arazu[supplication]; de[carry]
#tr.en: the leader …… prays …… in the @wTN{E-ŋa-ŋiš-šua}, her delightful residence, the awesome palace. 
#etcsl: line-id=1.A.A.30

